  "callout_language": "Gulf Arabic mixed with English military terms ('contact', 'reload', 'man down'); the UAE forces train closely with US, French and Australian advisers.",
  "doctrine": {
    "summary": "Small, highly funded and combat-experienced ('Little Sparta'): Emirati forces fought in Afghanistan alongside NATO and led ground operations in southern Yemen (2015-2019), relying on Presidential Guard and special forces, MRAP-heavy mechanised task forces, attack helicopters and large numbers of local proxy forces trained and paid by the UAE. Most of the army's manpower is expatriate-supported and conscription began in 2014. Strong in air defence, ISR drones and precision fires. In 2026 the UAE was among the Gulf states hit hardest by Iranian missile and drone strikes and struck back at Iran. It withdrew its remaining forces from Yemen at the end of December 2025 after a crisis with Saudi Arabia over the Southern Transitional Council.",
    "squad_size": 8,
    "fireteam": "Western-style 8-9 man section in two fireteams with a Minimi and grenadier, mounted in M-ATVs, Nimr Jais/Ajban or BMP-3s. Presidential Guard and special forces in 4-8 man teams with Western advisers. In game: 8 men in battle-buddy pairs.",
    "tactics": [
      "MRAP task forces (M-ATV, MaxxPro, Nimr) with heavy MGs and grenade launchers move fast along coastal roads",
      "Local partner forces lead infantry assaults; Emirati special forces direct fires and air support",
      "Apache gunships and armed drones overhead during ground operations",
      "Leclerc tanks and BMP-3s for the decisive push into towns",
      "Dense air and counter-drone defence of ports, bases and energy sites (persian_gulf_coast)"
    ],
